# Cursor AI Instructions

## Code Quality Standards

### NO COMMENTS POLICY
- NEVER write comments in code
- Focus on writing self-documenting, readable code instead
- Use descriptive variable names and function names
- Break complex logic into smaller, well-named functions
- Comments are a code smell - if you need to explain code with comments, the code isn't clear enough

### Code Style
- Write clean, readable code that speaks for itself
- Use meaningful names that describe intent
- Prefer explicit over implicit
- Keep functions small and focused
- Use TypeScript types to document interfaces and contracts

### When Code Needs Explanation
- Refactor the code to be more readable
- Extract complex logic into well-named functions
- Use descriptive variable names
- Consider if the code is doing too much (single responsibility principle)

Remember: Good code doesn't need comments to be understood.
